  "reviewNotes": [
    "These values are diagnostic/treatment decision thresholds from disease-specific clinical recommendations, not population reference intervals.",
    "Do not render this dataset under a generic 'normal laboratory ranges' label.",
    "Sepsis thresholds are nonspecific and the source explicitly frames neonatal sepsis as a clinical syndrome requiring combined clinical, laboratory and microbiological assessment.",
    "The neutropenia table is preserved by birth-weight and postnatal-age bands; do not merge it into a generic ANC reference range.",
    "Polycythemia treatment decisions are based on venous hematocrit; capillary/peripheral values are a trigger for confirmation, not an interchangeable measurement.",
    "Treatment action details are intentionally omitted from this compact threshold dataset and require the full recommendation/runtime clinical contract.",
    "Promotion requires clinician review of every comparator, boundary and source version."
  ]
